WEBVTT

00:00:03.504 --> 00:00:05.089
Say, Tsukimi...

00:00:06.215 --> 00:00:12.138
When you get married,
I'll make you a snow-white dress.

00:00:14.056 --> 00:00:17.852
A snow-white dress just like this jellyfish.

00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:28.237
It's beautiful...

00:00:29.238 --> 00:00:33.451
Please keep what I'm about to sing

00:00:34.911 --> 00:00:36.913
<i>Just between us, okay?</i>

00:00:36.996 --> 00:00:42.710
<i>The truth is, I want to keep my
desires hidden deep in my heart</i>

00:00:42.793 --> 00:00:44.837
<i>A secret, a secret</i>

00:01:01.145 --> 00:01:03.689
<i>I</i> want <i>to take shortcuts</i>

00:01:03.773 --> 00:01:07.568
<i>Never getting soaked by the rain</i>

00:01:07.652 --> 00:01:11.197
<i>Never getting knocked over by the wind</i>

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.992
<i>Even if that's being devious, smile</i>

00:01:15.076 --> 00:01:19.455
<i>Even if I'm a coward, play with me</i>

00:01:20.456 --> 00:01:23.042
<i>I don't</i> want <i>to feel sad</i>

00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:26.921
<i>Never getting soaked by tears</i>

00:01:27.004 --> 00:01:30.549
<i>Never feeling at my wit's end</i>

00:01:30.633 --> 00:01:34.053
<i>Just smile and think I'm insensitive</i>

00:01:34.136 --> 00:01:39.100
<i>Only tell me about fun things</i>

00:01:42.853 --> 00:01:47.400
<i>See, there are faces I</i> want <i>to
see and voices I</i> want <i>to hear</i>

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:52.238
<i>When I wake up I trumpet my joy:</i>

00:01:52.321 --> 00:01:58.286
Good morning!
Let's have another fine day!

00:01:58.286 --> 00:01:58.911
"Princess Jellyfish"

00:02:00.955 --> 00:02:02.581
It's beautiful...

00:02:02.665 --> 00:02:07.795
It's... It's almost like you're
the princess of the jellyfish!

00:02:07.878 --> 00:02:09.046
Just of the jellyfish?!

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:12.300
Okay, let's do a purple jelly next!

00:02:12.383 --> 00:02:14.218
What? Another one?

00:02:14.302 --> 00:02:18.681
Why don't we have some tea first?
Incidentally, is your father around...?

00:02:18.764 --> 00:02:20.599
Tsukimi...

00:02:20.683 --> 00:02:23.352
You've had a complete awakening, haven't you?!

00:02:23.436 --> 00:02:26.355
“Come again?
--I knew I wasn't mistaken about you!

00:02:26.439 --> 00:02:32.069
Make more, make more! Make as
many jellyfish dresses as you want!

00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:36.198
Oh, what a nice color! The same
pinkish-mauve as an immature purple jelly!

00:02:36.282 --> 00:02:39.452
Oh, my mom gave me that dress.

00:02:39.535 --> 00:02:40.661
May I?

00:02:40.745 --> 00:02:43.247
Oh? You want to give it a go? Okay...

00:02:43.331 --> 00:02:46.584
Wow! Thank you!

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:49.545
What? You're gonna give it a go right here?

00:02:49.628 --> 00:02:52.006
Oh, yes. That's the idea...

00:02:55.384 --> 00:02:57.803
Wait... when you say you'll "give
it a go," you mean with scissors?

00:02:57.887 --> 00:03:02.892
Purple jellies! Purple jellies!
Purple jellies are pink before they grow!

00:03:02.975 --> 00:03:03.934
--Purple jellies are teeny-tiny,

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:05.061
--Let's get out of here...
--Purple jellies are teeny-tiny,

00:03:05.061 --> 00:03:05.936
--Agreed...
--Purple jellies are teeny-tiny,

00:03:05.936 --> 00:03:08.773
--Agreed...
--but they hurt when they go stingy-stingy!

00:03:08.856 --> 00:03:11.150
Purple jellies! Purple jellies! Purple jellies...!

00:03:12.818 --> 00:03:16.364
Do you think it would be
all right if we visited again?

00:03:16.447 --> 00:03:20.242
I saw a photo of the late
lchiro Koibuchi on the wall.

00:03:20.326 --> 00:03:24.455
He's just my type, so I'd
really love to meet Keiichiro too...

00:03:24.538 --> 00:03:26.624
Perhaps we can pay another visit tomorrow.

00:03:26.707 --> 00:03:28.000
In a home that spacious,

00:03:28.084 --> 00:03:32.713
there must be a Taisho-style
room perfect for Midoriko and Umeko...

00:03:35.674 --> 00:03:37.259
It won't come off!

00:03:37.343 --> 00:03:39.804
Amamizu-kan...

00:03:39.887 --> 00:03:41.138
Umeko!

00:03:41.222 --> 00:03:44.392
Matsuko! Yoshibo! O-Take!

00:03:44.475 --> 00:03:45.267
Takeo!

00:03:45.351 --> 00:03:48.354
"Jellyfish of Dreams"

00:03:48.979 --> 00:03:52.566
Listen, I realize I was the one who
dragged you into the fashion world,

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:55.861
so I can live with the fact
that you've chopped up my dress

00:03:55.945 --> 00:03:57.780
to make your own cute jellyfish dress, but...

00:03:59.448 --> 00:04:01.909
"Sisterhood Mode"

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:04.620
<i>I</i> can't <i>believe Tsukimijust totally
ignored me. She's usually so timid...</i>

00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:08.249
<i>Tsukimi is fearsome in her fully awakened mode!</i>

00:04:08.332 --> 00:04:11.127
<i>Now that she's had an awakening,
Tsukimi can keep making more and more dresses</i>

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.796
<i>while I handle the brand strategy...</i>

00:04:13.879 --> 00:04:16.841
<i>I can see it all now...</i>

00:04:16.924 --> 00:04:19.385
<i>We'll open our first store
on New York's Fifth Avenue!</i>

00:04:19.468 --> 00:04:22.555
We'll have a <i>second</i> store
on Rue Saint-Honoré in Paris...

00:04:22.638 --> 00:04:26.308
And we'll launch our first
wholly-owned Japanese outlet in Ginza!

00:04:26.392 --> 00:04:28.769
<i>We've made it to the top...!</i>

00:04:28.853 --> 00:04:30.438
OVVVV!

00:04:33.065 --> 00:04:35.359
Huh? Didn't you go home?

00:04:35.443 --> 00:04:38.446
It's Amamizu-kan! It's...!

00:04:38.529 --> 00:04:40.281
Huh?

00:04:40.364 --> 00:04:45.578
'Tis all over! Guan Yu is no more!

00:04:45.661 --> 00:04:48.330
Th-Th-This can't <i>be...</i>

00:04:48.414 --> 00:04:49.623
Calm down!

00:04:49.707 --> 00:04:51.625
Chieko, have you called your mom?

00:04:51.709 --> 00:04:54.003
I've tried and tried, but she won't pick up.

00:04:54.086 --> 00:04:57.173
I knew it! Chiekds mother has been deceived!

00:04:57.256 --> 00:05:01.677
Curse you, Dong Zhuo!
You shall pay for this with your life!

00:05:05.764 --> 00:05:08.309
Ah, this is the place!

00:05:08.392 --> 00:05:09.894
Let's make this quick.

00:05:09.977 --> 00:05:11.645
Hold on there!

00:05:11.729 --> 00:05:14.773
Just what do you think you're
doing so early in the morning?

00:05:15.983 --> 00:05:19.403
We humble ourselves before you as before
Zhuge Liang! Please, grant us a little time!

00:05:19.487 --> 00:05:21.822
We can have everything
hauled out in ten minutes!

00:05:21.906 --> 00:05:24.492
My O gauge model railway is heavy,
so I'd like a little more time than that.

00:05:24.575 --> 00:05:29.205
Please! My babies are in there!
Before you demolish it, at least let me--!

00:05:29.288 --> 00:05:32.333
Demolish it? Oh, no, this isn't what you think.

00:05:32.416 --> 00:05:33.667
--Huh?
--What?

00:05:33.751 --> 00:05:37.338
Yeah, apparently he mixed up which
building we're supposed to demolish.

00:05:37.421 --> 00:05:40.424
I did check, honest! But then...

00:05:40.508 --> 00:05:44.053
Oh, if that's what you're
looking for--isn't that it there?

00:05:44.136 --> 00:05:47.473
We'll get the tarps off and
have it back to normal right away.

00:05:47.556 --> 00:05:49.808
Sorry for the trouble.

00:05:55.231 --> 00:06:01.445
Sounds like the place is vacant now.
They said all the residents have moved far away.

00:06:01.529 --> 00:06:03.322
This is...

00:06:04.323 --> 00:06:07.952
This is a really good shot.
Great work as always, Sugi, my man.

00:06:08.035 --> 00:06:10.579
Well, photography is my specialty.

00:06:13.707 --> 00:06:17.044
Please accept this as a token of
my apologies for all the trouble.

00:06:17.044 --> 00:06:17.795
"Confectionery WEST"

00:06:17.795 --> 00:06:19.004
Oh, how thoughtful of you!

00:06:19.088 --> 00:06:22.883
It must really be rough, though,
what with all the redevelopment plans.

00:06:22.967 --> 00:06:23.759
Pardon?

00:06:23.842 --> 00:06:26.679
I suppose this building's
coming down soon too, right?

00:06:31.433 --> 00:06:33.435
So Xuzhou has fallen as well...

00:06:33.519 --> 00:06:34.728
Excavator machines are really cool, too...

00:06:34.812 --> 00:06:38.983
That gentleman from the construction
company was a hunk, don't you think?

00:06:39.066 --> 00:06:43.112
They gave me some cookies
from WEST! Let's have some tea.

00:06:43.195 --> 00:06:44.488
Go WEST!

00:06:44.572 --> 00:06:48.200
--Is it the leaf pie set?
--Any almond tarts?

00:06:59.086 --> 00:07:00.588
Discuss what?

00:07:00.671 --> 00:07:02.298
Hello, Mother?

00:07:02.381 --> 00:07:05.217
Mother? Hello?!

00:07:05.301 --> 00:07:06.927
We got cut off.

00:07:07.011 --> 00:07:08.554
What did she want to say?

00:07:08.637 --> 00:07:13.976
She said she had something
important to discuss about Amamizu-kan...

00:07:14.059 --> 00:07:16.353
This is all taking a turn for the worse...

00:07:16.437 --> 00:07:18.606
Tidings of unconditional surrender?!

00:07:18.689 --> 00:07:23.485
I guess now our only choice is to be
live-in workers at the Yamanaka Hot Spring.

00:07:23.569 --> 00:07:25.487
Just like in that show Haru-chan...

00:07:30.117 --> 00:07:34.330
Ms. Inari. Are you trying
to empty the coffeemaker?

00:07:34.413 --> 00:07:35.998
Oh, my! Whatever am I thinking?

00:07:36.081 --> 00:07:37.583
Ouch, hot!

00:07:37.666 --> 00:07:41.670
What's the matter? Did something happen?

00:07:41.754 --> 00:07:43.547
"Happen"?

00:07:47.885 --> 00:07:50.179
You've been working a little too hard lately.

00:07:50.262 --> 00:07:52.765
Maybe you should take some time off.

00:07:52.848 --> 00:07:57.519
My brother should be back pretty soon.
I guess I'll take this over there...

00:07:57.603 --> 00:08:00.814
Kuranosuke!

00:08:00.898 --> 00:08:05.235
Kuranosuke! Kuranosuke!

00:08:06.153 --> 00:08:08.656
Th-The Burmese Harp?

00:08:08.739 --> 00:08:13.494
Mizushima! Let's go back to
Japan--no, that's not the issue!

00:08:13.577 --> 00:08:16.830
Amamizu-kan's going to be torn to pieces!

00:08:16.914 --> 00:08:19.124
Huh? I thought that was just a mix-up.

00:08:19.208 --> 00:08:22.044
This is perfect timing, though.
We still need to finish that one dress--

00:08:22.127 --> 00:08:24.630
They're going to tear it down!

00:08:24.713 --> 00:08:28.634
We have to make jellyfish dolls...
Lots of them, and quick.

00:08:28.717 --> 00:08:31.345
And then we have to buy Amamizu-kan!

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:43.107
--A hole! A hole in my finger!
--Use a thimble.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:46.276
For now, we'll shoot for
20 dolls per person per day.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.946
100 a day. 1,000 in ten days!

00:08:49.029 --> 00:08:50.030
Can we really do it?

00:08:50.114 --> 00:08:54.243
We have no other choice.
This is really all we can do...

00:08:54.326 --> 00:08:56.412
--I cannot!
--Talk about giving up fast!

00:08:56.495 --> 00:08:59.540
My right hand! It refuses to do as I say!

00:08:59.623 --> 00:09:02.543
--If only I could use it...!
--Sounds like you just lost interest to me.

00:09:02.626 --> 00:09:05.838
I agree. You haven't even made one yet!

00:09:05.921 --> 00:09:07.673
What we can do...?

00:09:08.674 --> 00:09:10.008
Wait!

00:09:10.092 --> 00:09:12.261
There is a way...

00:09:15.556 --> 00:09:16.348
Stylish magazines!

00:09:16.432 --> 00:09:19.810
Legend has it touching these will
make you horribly trendy in an instant!

00:09:19.893 --> 00:09:21.603
Do you have any copies of Railway Journal?

00:09:21.687 --> 00:09:25.691
We're gonna send in applications for
every model-wanted ad and audition in these.

00:09:25.774 --> 00:09:27.067
Take photos with this.

00:09:27.151 --> 00:09:28.819
Panning technique!

00:09:30.028 --> 00:09:33.490
We're gonna have people in the
fashion industry see Tsukimi's dresses.

00:09:33.574 --> 00:09:35.033
Someone's gonna love 'em, I just know it.

00:09:35.117 --> 00:09:37.286
And if all goes well, we'll
build a business out of them!

00:09:37.369 --> 00:09:38.996
Th-The jellyfish dresses?

00:09:39.079 --> 00:09:40.748
What's the point?

00:09:40.831 --> 00:09:43.292
A piece of clothing costs 5,000 yen at most.

00:09:43.375 --> 00:09:47.379
In fact, these fine garments of mine
go for around 1,480 yen at Super Maruko!

00:09:47.463 --> 00:09:48.630
Are you shocked?!

00:09:48.714 --> 00:09:51.049
Fancy clothes fetch high prices!

00:09:51.133 --> 00:09:53.594
We're talking hundreds of
thousands of yen, or even more!

00:09:53.677 --> 00:09:55.512
Don't you know anything
about brand-name goods?

00:09:55.596 --> 00:09:56.805
Brand-name?

00:09:56.889 --> 00:10:00.476
--Wait, like Louis <i>Llll</i> or whoever...?
--Louis Vuitton.

00:10:00.559 --> 00:10:03.479
My dresses...? You can't be serious...

00:10:03.562 --> 00:10:05.230
lam!

00:10:05.314 --> 00:10:08.734
If I'm right, they <i>will</i>
catch a professionaPs attention.

00:10:08.817 --> 00:10:12.237
So you need to make dresses. Lots of 'em!

00:10:16.408 --> 00:10:17.659
Hiya!

00:10:17.743 --> 00:10:19.286
Oh, Sara, my girl!

00:10:19.369 --> 00:10:22.623
You're looking just fabulous!
You're a modern-day Muse!

00:10:22.706 --> 00:10:24.500
Still popping over to
Yokohama every chance you get?

00:10:24.583 --> 00:10:28.337
Of course. That's where the action is!
Bashamichi! Chinatown!

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:30.422
Just don't make too much
of a spectacle of yourself.

00:10:30.506 --> 00:10:32.508
You're our top model, after all.

00:10:32.591 --> 00:10:34.802
Are those applications for the contest?

00:10:34.885 --> 00:10:38.847
Yeah. A whole lot came in! Wanna take a look?

00:10:47.773 --> 00:10:49.983
Afro!

00:10:50.609 --> 00:10:51.610
It's commercial time!

00:10:51.693 --> 00:10:52.986
Clara!

00:10:53.987 --> 00:10:55.072
It's the second half!

00:10:55.155 --> 00:10:55.989
Tequila!

00:10:58.575 --> 00:11:01.411
<i>How many years has it been
since I've had</i> a <i>one-sided crush?</i>

00:11:02.955 --> 00:11:05.415
<i>But no, I've got to push it out of my mind...</i>

00:11:25.477 --> 00:11:28.146
<i>Whew, that was scary. I thought
it was payback time for sure--</i>

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:30.107
Shu-Shu, it is you!

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:31.692
Prime Minister...

00:11:31.775 --> 00:11:35.487
We're in private company
now! Call me Negi-pyon!

00:11:35.571 --> 00:11:36.780
What can I do for you?

00:11:36.864 --> 00:11:41.076
Everyone stopped talking to
me once my support fell below 5%,

00:11:41.159 --> 00:11:43.287
so I thought I'd go have some fun on my own.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:47.165
Oh, right! I've got an extra ticket!
You should come with me, Shu-Shu.

00:11:47.249 --> 00:11:50.961
What? But, I...

00:11:59.553 --> 00:12:01.597
So many Stylish...

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:05.601
Stay strong. This is for Amamizu-kan.

00:12:05.684 --> 00:12:07.811
Still, these clothes, this atmosphere...

00:12:07.895 --> 00:12:10.772
--I can't adapt! Not to this!
--Oh!

00:12:10.856 --> 00:12:15.444
Oh! The three of you look adorable!
You're modern-day Muses!

00:12:16.945 --> 00:12:18.488
Afro...?

00:12:18.572 --> 00:12:21.116
“Afro?
--I cannot adapt!

00:12:21.199 --> 00:12:22.576
Afro!

00:12:22.659 --> 00:12:25.120
--I'm getting dizzy...!
--Afro!

00:12:29.041 --> 00:12:30.417
Are we good to go?

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:31.501
Yes...

00:12:31.585 --> 00:12:34.963
Um, but... are you really sure about this?

00:12:35.047 --> 00:12:35.756
Huh?

00:12:35.797 --> 00:12:39.509
I mean, this is my very
first time making clothes,

00:12:39.593 --> 00:12:43.055
and everyone else around us
looks so much more put-together...

00:12:43.138 --> 00:12:45.891
--Plus...
--You're <i>still</i> talking like that?

00:12:45.974 --> 00:12:48.769
You'll be fine. Trust me.

00:12:48.852 --> 00:12:51.104
Oh, Kura-honey! Hiya!

00:12:51.188 --> 00:12:54.900
Ah, a princess! You're a modern-day Muse!

00:12:54.983 --> 00:12:56.026
Thanks.

00:12:56.109 --> 00:12:57.986
Good morning!

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:01.949
Oh! How beautiful! You're a modern-day Muse!

00:13:02.032 --> 00:13:04.785
Whoa! Is this a new dress?

00:13:04.868 --> 00:13:06.536
Huh?

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:09.373
Who might this girl be?

00:13:09.456 --> 00:13:12.334
Oh, she's Tsukimi, the girl
I told you about the other day.

00:13:12.417 --> 00:13:18.090
She designed these dresses.
They're part of a brand we just launched.

00:13:18.173 --> 00:13:21.593
A b-brand?! But I've only made two...!

00:13:21.677 --> 00:13:23.804
How do you expect to succeed
if we don't start working it here?

00:13:23.887 --> 00:13:24.763
But...

00:13:24.846 --> 00:13:27.432
Your dress is totally cute!

00:13:27.516 --> 00:13:28.767
Isn't it, though?

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:29.685
Huh? Wham?

00:13:29.768 --> 00:13:30.978
Who's that?! She's way cute!

00:13:31.061 --> 00:13:32.980
I wish my dress was like that...

00:13:33.063 --> 00:13:35.357
I'm so jealous...

00:13:37.025 --> 00:13:43.490
Next is entry #12! Kurumi Ebihara
from Miyazaki Prefecture!

00:13:43.573 --> 00:13:46.243
Next is entry #13!

00:13:46.326 --> 00:13:46.952
--Emiri Machida from Kanagawa Prefecture!

00:13:46.952 --> 00:13:48.704
--Where's Kurako?
--Emiri Machida from Kanagawa Prefecture!

00:13:48.787 --> 00:13:52.165
She better not be eating
something tasty backstage...

00:13:52.249 --> 00:13:53.291
Mom...

00:13:53.375 --> 00:13:54.001
--Next is entry #14!

00:13:54.001 --> 00:13:56.253
--I'm so nervous that my heart might just
leap out of my mouth. --Next is entry #14!

00:13:56.253 --> 00:13:58.422
--I'm so nervous that my heart might just leap out
of my mouth. --Erika Higa from Okinawa Prefecture!

00:13:58.422 --> 00:14:00.048
--But, for some reason, <i>I</i> don't feel the urge to
run away, --Erika Higa from Okinawa Prefecture!

00:14:00.048 --> 00:14:01.842
--But, for some reason, <i>I</i> don't feel the
urge to run away, --Next is entry #15!

00:14:01.842 --> 00:14:03.427
<i>--Even though I'm sure my old self would have
run outside by now...</i> --Next <i>is</i> entry <i>#1</i> 5!

00:14:03.427 --> 00:14:06.763
--Even though I'm sure my old self would have run outside
by now... --Minako Noto from lshikawa prefecture!

00:14:06.847 --> 00:14:09.433
<i>Could it be because hem'?</i>

00:14:09.516 --> 00:14:10.350
Let's make one!

00:14:10.434 --> 00:14:12.728
Let's make a jellyfish dress!

00:14:13.353 --> 00:14:19.151
Next is entry #35! Kurako Amamizu from Tokyo!

00:14:19.234 --> 00:14:20.402
Amamizu?

00:14:20.485 --> 00:14:23.780
That wretch! She took Amamizu-kan's
name without even asking!

00:14:29.619 --> 00:14:31.246
Mom...

00:14:36.585 --> 00:14:38.170
I...

00:14:39.087 --> 00:14:41.715
If there's a nice vacation
home I'm gonna buy it,

00:14:41.798 --> 00:14:43.425
so I'll count on you for
the estimates and stuff, okay?

00:14:43.508 --> 00:14:44.926
All right.

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:46.303
Okey-dokey, then!

00:14:46.386 --> 00:14:49.765
He loves me. He loves me not. He loves me.

00:14:49.848 --> 00:14:51.641
He loves me not...

00:14:53.518 --> 00:14:56.188
Another one. One with lots of petals this time!

00:14:56.271 --> 00:14:58.356
C-Certainly!

00:15:02.527 --> 00:15:04.905
P-Please give my glasses back.

00:15:04.988 --> 00:15:09.034
Chieko, get the pink dress.
The one Tsukimi made.

00:15:09.117 --> 00:15:09.826
This?

00:15:09.868 --> 00:15:11.995
Yeah. Now put it on her.

00:15:12.079 --> 00:15:14.414
P-Put it on?! I can't do that!

00:15:14.498 --> 00:15:16.500
My ancestors would be ashamed of me,

00:15:16.583 --> 00:15:17.375
--wearing a naked-shoulder dress like that!

00:15:17.375 --> 00:15:19.377
--Call it "strapless."
--wearing a naked-shoulder dress like that!

00:15:19.461 --> 00:15:23.548
I'd rather slit my belly and
perish this instant than wear it.

00:15:23.632 --> 00:15:24.966
Chieko, assist me!

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:29.721
Understood. But at least try it
on before resorting to seppuku.

00:15:29.805 --> 00:15:32.265
Why should I have to wear it anyway?!

00:15:32.349 --> 00:15:34.810
We're #1 in every category by a landslide!

00:15:34.893 --> 00:15:37.771
The designer can't just slink back home now!

00:15:37.854 --> 00:15:42.192
Jiji, I'll hold her down. You put it on her.

00:15:42.275 --> 00:15:43.443
Right.

00:15:43.527 --> 00:15:45.529
Huh? Wham?

00:15:45.612 --> 00:15:47.781
No!

00:15:47.864 --> 00:15:50.909
Oh, no! The zipper won't fasten!

00:15:50.992 --> 00:15:52.369
Yikes! You serious?!

00:15:52.452 --> 00:15:55.831
Plus, her upper arms are pretty flabby...

00:15:56.998 --> 00:15:59.000
Kill me... Kill me, please!

00:15:59.084 --> 00:16:04.172
Don't worry, I'll sew you a stole
right now. Oh, look, we even have fur!

00:16:04.256 --> 00:16:06.049
How will you hold it in place? Safety pins?

00:16:06.133 --> 00:16:07.759
Hmm, good question...

00:16:11.054 --> 00:16:14.391
Um... Uh, where are we...?

00:16:14.474 --> 00:16:16.268
All right. Now wait right here.

00:16:16.351 --> 00:16:20.480
Wait? Um, what's going on?

00:16:20.564 --> 00:16:23.150
Oh, I forgot! The brand's name...

00:16:23.233 --> 00:16:23.900
Huh?

00:16:23.942 --> 00:16:26.361
Crap! What do we do? Let me think...

00:16:26.444 --> 00:16:30.323
Finally, let's bring out the winners
of the top score in all categories:

00:16:30.407 --> 00:16:35.871
Kurako Amamizu and
Tsukimi Kurashita, her designer.

00:16:35.954 --> 00:16:37.497
Come on out!

00:16:37.581 --> 00:16:38.498
Here we go.

00:16:38.582 --> 00:16:40.167
Huh?!

00:16:47.507 --> 00:16:50.927
Wh-What...? A jellyfish...?

00:16:52.012 --> 00:16:54.389
Say, Tsukimi...

00:16:54.472 --> 00:17:01.897
All girls can be beautiful
princesses when they grow up.

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:03.773
Princesses...!

00:17:10.113 --> 00:17:13.950
Now for our lovely presenter, Sara!

00:17:14.034 --> 00:17:16.244
What's the brand's name?

00:17:16.328 --> 00:17:17.746
Umm...

00:17:17.829 --> 00:17:21.333
Hey, what kind of animal is Clara in English?

00:17:21.416 --> 00:17:23.960
Huh? Oh, in English?

00:17:24.044 --> 00:17:26.630
Jelly... fish...

00:17:26.713 --> 00:17:28.381
Then we'll go with that!

00:17:35.013 --> 00:17:38.516
Who dares plunder my meat?!

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:40.393
That's what you get for dillydallying.

00:17:40.477 --> 00:17:42.229
I am not dillydallying!

00:17:42.312 --> 00:17:45.857
--| simply prefer my meat well-done!
--Oh, this is ready.

00:17:45.941 --> 00:17:47.734
--You haven't eaten at all, Tsukimi.
--Damn you! At this rate,

00:17:47.734 --> 00:17:48.109
--You haven't eaten at all, Tsukimi.
--I'll never get to eat meat for as long as I live!

00:17:48.109 --> 00:17:49.486
--This is Matsusaka beef, you know.
--I'll never get to eat meat for as long as I live!

00:17:49.486 --> 00:17:50.237
--I'm sorry. I'm just not very hungry...
--I'll never get to eat meat for as long as I live!

00:17:50.237 --> 00:17:51.655
--I'm sorry. I'm just not very hungry...
--I prefer my meat rare.

00:17:51.655 --> 00:17:52.197
--I'm sorry. I'm just not very hungry...
--| can eat mine not even cooked.

00:17:52.197 --> 00:17:53.240
--Is something wrong?
--| can eat mine not even cooked.

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:53.657
--Is something wrong?
--Oh, why was I cursed

00:17:53.657 --> 00:17:55.659
--Yes... I had a near-death experience
--Oh, why was I cursed

00:17:55.659 --> 00:17:57.410
--Yes... I had a near-death experience
--with this preference for well-done meat?!

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:59.454
--Just a little while ago...
--with this preference for well-done meat?!

00:17:59.537 --> 00:18:00.538
Huh?

00:18:00.622 --> 00:18:03.291
First, I climbed up along,
long staircase in the pitch dark,

00:18:03.375 --> 00:18:08.129
and then suddenly a door opened
and I was surrounded by a bright light...

00:18:08.213 --> 00:18:10.257
Am I dead?

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:12.550
They don't have yakiniku in heaven.

00:18:12.634 --> 00:18:15.387
Ms. Mejiro requested seconds.

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:17.973
Oh, <i>I'll</i> do it, then...

00:18:18.056 --> 00:18:19.724
Mom...

00:18:19.808 --> 00:18:27.107
<i>According to everyone else, I stood up on
the stage and was introduced as a designer.</i>

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:33.697
<i>But all I remember is Kuranosuke asking
me what jellyfish are called in English...</i>

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:37.742
<i>...and the feeling of my
hand being held tightly.</i>

00:18:41.288 --> 00:18:43.290
I guess it'd be better to have
a pro come up with something,

00:18:43.373 --> 00:18:46.084
but I don't wanna spend
a ton of money, either...

00:18:46.167 --> 00:18:48.295
Then allow me to figure it out!

00:18:49.713 --> 00:18:53.842
I've completed it!
Everyone, give a shout of triumph!

00:18:53.842 --> 00:18:55.885
"Jellius Fishicus"

00:18:55.885 --> 00:18:55.927
What kind of clothes are you thinking of?

00:18:55.927 --> 00:18:59.139
"Jelly"

00:18:59.139 --> 00:18:59.180
Don't stick a random train in!

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:02.517
"Jelly Fish"

00:19:02.517 --> 00:19:02.684
Don't make it look like a café sign, either!

00:19:02.767 --> 00:19:05.603
Then, putting everyone's opinions
together, what do you think of this?

00:19:05.603 --> 00:19:07.856
"Jelly Fish"

00:19:07.856 --> 00:19:08.398
That doesn't have a speck
of anyone else's opinion in it!

00:19:08.481 --> 00:19:12.736
Get serious, will you? Our goal is
to get into a Mode é Paris someday!

00:19:12.819 --> 00:19:14.029
A " moldy pari-pari"?

00:19:14.112 --> 00:19:16.156
What are you talking about?

00:19:16.239 --> 00:19:18.950
You know, like in the commercial for
the super-thin "pari-pari" rice crackers!

00:19:19.034 --> 00:19:21.995
Ugh, it's pointless to talk about it here.

00:19:22.078 --> 00:19:23.288
Tsukimi?

00:19:23.371 --> 00:19:24.956
Huh?

00:19:30.795 --> 00:19:32.964
Oh, here you are.

00:19:33.965 --> 00:19:36.676
Yuck, this wig stinks like meat...

00:19:39.846 --> 00:19:43.475
Geez. Get used to it already, will you?

00:19:43.558 --> 00:19:46.144
L-I'm fine as long as
I don't look directly at you...

00:19:46.227 --> 00:19:49.731
Come on, now. You gotta learn
to look at me when I'm not in drag.

00:19:49.814 --> 00:19:53.109
We share a common destiny now, you know.

00:19:57.572 --> 00:20:01.785
<i>Wh-What am I saying?!
And what am I feeling bashful for?!</i>

00:20:01.868 --> 00:20:04.996
Um, can I ask you something?

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:06.831
Wh-What is it?

00:20:06.915 --> 00:20:10.460
Do you think this will really work out well?

00:20:11.544 --> 00:20:14.214
It will. It'll turn out great.

00:20:17.509 --> 00:20:19.177
Mother...

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.137
Two Chiekos...

00:20:21.221 --> 00:20:22.138
Twins?

00:20:22.222 --> 00:20:25.308
No! She is Chieko's honorable mother!

00:20:25.392 --> 00:20:29.187
My phone was stomped on and broken
at an event with my darling Yon-sama.

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:35.068
So... you said you needed to
talk to me about Amamizu-kan...

00:20:35.151 --> 00:20:38.196
Yes, about that...

00:20:38.321 --> 00:20:42.117
--Give us a little time! --I'll have no place for my Takeo
collection if you kick us out...! --Please, Mother! Reconsider!

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:44.786
Oh? You think I should sell it after all?

00:20:44.869 --> 00:20:45.620
Huh?

00:20:45.662 --> 00:20:48.832
Yon-sama decided to use
Japan as his base for a while,

00:20:48.915 --> 00:20:52.669
so I came here to tell you I don't
need to sell the building anymore!

00:20:52.752 --> 00:20:54.295
Mother...

00:20:54.379 --> 00:20:57.424
But if you think I should reconsider, I will!

00:20:57.507 --> 00:20:58.007
--Wait--!
--Halt!

00:20:58.007 --> 00:20:59.717
--Mom... --VVait--! --Halt!

00:20:59.843 --> 00:21:03.763
<i>--Hold on! Hold on! --It's already been six months since
I left for Tokyo to try to make it as an illustrator.</i>

00:21:03.847 --> 00:21:08.601
<i>The metropolis of Tokyo works in
mysterious ways. It's one mystery after another.</i>

00:21:08.685 --> 00:21:12.605
<i>I think this city must be made of mysteries.</i>

00:21:12.605 --> 00:21:13.064
"How about this?"

00:21:13.064 --> 00:21:16.901
<i>So I have no doubt that many more
mysteries are just around the corner.</i>

00:21:18.653 --> 00:21:20.238
They sure are!

00:21:21.281 --> 00:21:30.290
<i>I really want you to
realize that you're gorgeous</i>

00:21:30.373 --> 00:21:34.711
<i>Why haven't you realized it before this?</i>

00:21:34.794 --> 00:21:39.215
<i>It's like you've lost your heart</i>

00:21:39.299 --> 00:21:48.391
<i>I</i> want you to realize <i>it</i> right away,
right away, <i>I</i> want you to understand

00:21:48.475 --> 00:22:02.864
<i>I want you to realize it right</i> away,
<i>I want you to realize your beauty</i>

00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:08.703
<i>Because you're so very beautiful</i>

00:22:08.786 --> 00:22:12.790
<i>I want to convey that to you</i>

00:22:12.874 --> 00:22:22.467
<i>Your loveliness, forever and ever</i>

00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:30.892
<i>I'll be so happy if you'll
just realize your loveliness</i>

00:22:30.975 --> 00:22:35.688
<i>I</i> care about you, you know

00:22:35.772 --> 00:22:45.031
Please, realize your beauty
